251 0 obj
<< /A 862 0 R /ActualText (Diagram illustrating a boundary-aware network architecture for image segmentation. It includes components like Sobel kernel convolutions, boundary and region-aware decoders, and segmentation heads. Labels indicate layers such as conv stem, transformer block, and feature fusing. Arrows depict data flow, with annotations explaining batch size, channel dimensions, and image features. Definitions clarify elements like CFM \(Complementary Fusion Module\) and feature fusing.\r\n) /Alt (Diagram illustrating a boundary-aware network architecture for image segmentation. It includes components like Sobel kernel convolutions, boundary and region-aware decoders, and segmentation heads. Labels indicate layers such as conv stem, transformer block, and feature fusing. Arrows depict data flow, with annotations explaining batch size, channel dimensions, and image features. Definitions clarify elements like CFM \(Complementary Fusion Module\) and feature fusing.\r\n) /K 0 /P 104 0 R /Pg 235 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
252 0 obj
<< /A 863 0 R /ActualText (Diagram comparing ResNet34 and Mix Transformer architectures. ResNet34 uses convolutional layers with varying dimensions and strides, while Mix Transformer employs stages with OverlapPatchEmbed and Mix Transformer Blocks. The Mix Transformer Block involves multi-head attention, linear projections, Scaled Dot-product Attention, concatenation, depth-wise convolution, and GELU activation. The diagram includes labels and dimensions, highlighting the differences between the two models.\r\n) /Alt (Diagram comparing ResNet34 and Mix Transformer architectures. ResNet34 uses convolutional layers with varying dimensions and strides, while Mix Transformer employs stages with OverlapPatchEmbed and Mix Transformer Blocks. The Mix Transformer Block involves multi-head attention, linear projections, Scaled Dot-product Attention, concatenation, depth-wise convolution, and GELU activation. The diagram includes labels and dimensions, highlighting the differences between the two models.\r\n) /K 0 /P 104 0 R /Pg 236 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
